THOUGHT: The METHOD_NO_INIT error is about the constructor not guaranteeing initialization of keyFrames on all paths. The simplest way to satisfy NullAway without changing behavior is to ensure the field is initialized before any method that might throw, and to avoid passing a possibly null varargs array directly to setKeyFrames. I’ll modify the varargs constructor so it normalizes a null keyFrames parameter to an empty array, assigns the field directly, and computes animationDuration, mirroring setKeyFrames’ logic. Then I’ll run the Java compilation with NullAway to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '97,100c\  public Animation(float frameDuration, T... keyFrames) {
    this.frameDuration = frameDuration;
    if (keyFrames == null) {
      this.keyFrames = (T[]) new Object[0];
    } else {
      this.keyFrames = keyFrames;
    }
    this.animationDuration = this.keyFrames.length * frameDuration;
  }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/g2d/Animation.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway:|error(s)\]" new_build_output.log | tail -n 5```

